    "finding": "Not eligible for the National Register, the California Register or City Landmark designation",
    "address_as_surveyed": "23–25 Brompton Avenue",
    "apn_as_surveyed": "Block 6744, Lot 030",
    "note": "One of eight parcels the evaluation surveyed intensively, and one of five buildings the proposed Diamond/Bosworth infill site would demolish. Surveyed with 23 Brompton Avenue as one property on Lot 030, which has since been split. Built as a single-family home and described as a late example of the false-front vernacular wood-frame building put up in Glen Park from the turn of the century, altered by replacement cladding, a garage cut into the middle of the facade and boarded windows."
